steps.say:
Here is a method with one parameter, and a call that hands it one argument:
static void heal(int hp) { hp = hp + 10; }
int health = 50;
heal(health);
hp is the parameter: a local variable that belongs to heal. health is the argument: what the call hands over.

beats.code:
static void heal(int hp) {
    hp = hp + 10;
}

int health = 50;
heal(health);

steps.say:
To get the 60 out, the method has to return it and the caller has to store it:
static int heal(int hp) { return hp + 10; }
health = heal(health);
The pattern: a parameter is a copy. A change travels back to the caller only through return.

